Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:26:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Native plant runs for the Mallory baseline: every fault
 marker observed, a plant-run command, TARGET rows

The Mallory baseline drives fault trials as native runs of a case's workload
on its SEED's recording weave, planting faults as REPRODUCE does, and reads
GraphChecker's graph of each run (schedule.jsonl, the trace's exchanges).

- RecordingPlant: with -Dcausynth.plant.observe=true a planted run states
  every fault marker it evaluates (PLANT_MARKER: root name, call site and
  enclosing occurrence ids innermost first), so a driver can plant a FAULT
  row at any marker invocation an earlier run reached; marker() reads the
  enclosing occurrences once.
- explore/TargetRows: a plant's TARGET rows for the declared target
  occurrence, as ConfirmMain writes them (PLANT_FATAL atAnchor is the oracle).
- run_engine.sh plant-run <run dir> <plant> [bound]: one native planted run
  (run_configured_workload on analysis_classes_dir); campaign_stop_after=PLAN
  stops once PLAN resolved the declared target (the schedule index's
  target.occurrenceId).
- experiments/lib/run.sh writes the output's declared-target.yaml once,
  through a file of the writer's own: runs side by side share it.

Checked on hbase-bugs-backup-lock-reply-lost: a TARGET-only plant ran 16 s
with 216 PLANT_MARKER rows and no PLANT_FATAL; planting GraphChecker's one
FAULT root (RpcConnection#finishCall's RESPONSE) stated PLANT_FATAL atAnchor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
